    {
      "id": "tour:apply-command",
      "title": "How xpl checks and applies guide edits",
      "summary": "The `xpl apply` command reads a patch, loads the guide and its source index, and asks core to check the proposed merge. Core checks source anchors and protects reader-owned fields. The CLI writes the guide only after a successful result with changes; this tour leaves out later export checks.",
      "steps": [
        {
